WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:55.260
<b>Adventure 
in the Kingdom of Sand</b>

3
00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.550
Ah! What a nice breeze!

4
00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:12.660
[VIVI]
Nami, if you don't mind,
I'd like to stop the ship here.

5
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.330
It'll just be for a moment.

6
00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.000
Stop? What for?

7
00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.650
I have a very important mission for Karoo.

8
00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:20.370
Karoo?

9
00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.880
Karoo, I need you to go to Alubarna Palace

10
00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.750
and deliver this letter to my father.

11
00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:35.410
It contains everything uncovered
by Igaram and myself.

12
00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:39.150
for this country are in here.

13
00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.150
Also, it lets him know

14
00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:43.620
that I've returned to
Alabasta safe and sound

15
00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.620
and in the company
of brave friends

16
00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.200
willing to help us
in our struggle.

17
00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.270
Well, then. Can you do
this for me, Karoo?

18
00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.870
[squawks]

19
00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:57.710
Now, be careful to conserve
your water, 'kay?

20
00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:58.710
[KAROO squawks]

21
00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.780
Good luck! You can do it, Duck!

22
00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.720
Go let my father know, Karoo.

23
00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.450
There's hope for this
kingdom at last!

24
00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.320
[squawks]

25
00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:12.590
[VIVI]
I said "conserve,"
not "consume"!

26
00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:20.240
Thank you. And good luck.

27
00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:24.920
Well, I did know that Crocodile
was here in Alabasta...

28
00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:27.320
but him trying to
steal a kingdom?

29
00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.420
That sounds like a bad joke.

30
00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:32.000
Because why would a pirate
drop anchor in one spot

31
00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:33.030
and settle down?

32
00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.430
Crocodile trying to usurp
the throne of Alabasta

33
00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.270
doesn't make sense.

34
00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.240
[LUFFY]
All right! Let's set sail!

35
00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.210
[USOPP]
Hold on!

36
00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:42.020
[ACE]
You know, there
could be another side

37
00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:44.450
to this takeover thing.

38
00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:45.380
Huh?

39
00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:48.920
Like some sort of deeper goal or something.

40
00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:50.730
[LUFFY]
We're finally here!

41
00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.470
[CHOPPER]
Wow, so we're
going into the desert?

42
00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.400
Does anyone know how hot it's supposed to get?

43
00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.270
[NAMI]
Over a hundred
degrees in the daytime!

44
00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:58.460
[CHOPPER]
What?! Please
tell me you're joking!

45
00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:01.960
Ah! Nami, what happened?!
Where's your dancer outfit?!

46
00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:05.350
Ah! You too?! Vivi,
why are you wearing that?!

47
00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:08.180
Because any exposed skin will get sunburned.

48
00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.280
You have to cover up in the desert.

49
00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:14.050
But... those outfits...
were so sexy...

50
00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:15.190
[VIVI]
Put these on, Luffy.

51
00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:16.760
[LUFFY]
Oh, thank you.

52
00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:17.950
[ZORO]
Time to drop anchor.

53
00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:19.110
[USOPP]
Right.

54
00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.280
[splash]

55
00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:30.280
[LUFFY]
Yuba, here we come!

56
00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:33.860
[ZORO]
Huh?

57
00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.360
What are those?

58
00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:41.800
[DUGONGS yell]

59
00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:42.870
Turtles?

60
00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.040
No, I think they're seals.

61
00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:45.620
Kung Fu Dugongs!

62
00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:46.520
[CHOPPER]
"If you wanna come ashore,

63
00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:49.170
you'll have to beat me first,

64
00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:52.110
but I doubt that'll happen,
you buncha cowards!"

65
00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:53.440
he says.

66
00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:55.480
[USOPP]
Ha.

67
00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:58.510
Nobody calls me a coward
and gets away with it.

68
00:04:58.550 --> 00:04:59.880
Here comes the pain!

69
00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.180
[VIVI]
Usopp! No, wait!

70
00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:05.850
Kung Fu Dugongs
are really strong!

71
00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:07.020
[LUFFY yells]

72
00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:08.720
[LUFFY]
See! They're not too tough!

73
00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:10.820
[VIVI]
That's bad too!

74
00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:16.400
[LUFFY]
Huh? What the–

75
00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:17.630
It's one of their rules.

76
00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:21.270
If they lose a kung fu match,
they become the winner's pupil.

77
00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.140
You don't say...

78
00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:27.230
They think you're their master now!

79
00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:29.270
Right! Everyone, after me!

80
00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:30.700
Now, punch!

81
00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:33.390
No! Like this!

82
00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:36.120
Yeah! Now... harder!

83
00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:38.560
And now... left!

84
00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:40.730
Left! Right!

85
00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:44.760
Yeah!

86
00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:51.280
[LUFFY]
Hope all you guys
enjoy the food! See ya!

87
00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:54.280
"All you guys." "Food."
Now do you get it?

88
00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:56.250
No. They said they
wanted to go with us,

89
00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:57.320
so why couldn't we let 'em?

90
00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:58.700
We don't have enough
food and water

91
00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:00.760
to take care of
a group that big!

92
00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:01.790
Moron!

93
00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:03.350
Honestly, I don't know
what we would've done

94
00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:05.720
if Chopper hadn't
persuaded them to stay.

95
00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:06.890
[CHOPPER]
Yeah!

96
00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:09.110
They kept saying, "Where you
go, we'll follow, Master!"

97
00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:10.180
They really would have, too,

98
00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.810
if I hadn't given
them that food!

99
00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:14.340
[SANJI]
And now our food supply's
gotten a lot smaller.

100
00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:16.480
Thanks, Luffy, thanks.

101
00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:17.480
He's a handful.

102
00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.350
[SANJI]
You're tellin' me.

103
00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:23.920
[ZORO]
Hm?

104
00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:25.020
[USOPP]
Huh?

105
00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:30.890
[SANJI]
What's this?

106
00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:33.350
[LUFFY]
Are we in Yuba already?

107
00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:36.580
No. This is Erumalu.

108
00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:39.690
It was known far and wide
as the "City of Green."

109
00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.810
It was green?

110
00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:44.020
Take a good look around, everyone.

111
00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:47.890
This is what Baroque Works
has been doing to my country.

112
00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:51.860
The people of Alabasta, this is
what they've had to go through.

113
00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:57.560
[LUFFY]
Wow! There's nothing
here at all anymore, huh?

114
00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:58.390
[VIVI]
No.

115
00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:00.560
It's nothing but a ghost town now.

116
00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:03.400
But up until a few short years
ago, it was a thriving city

117
00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:07.000
full of gardens, palm trees,
and lush greenery.

118
00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:09.620
[ZORO]
This place? Hm.

119
00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.700
[VIVI]
Rain was always scarce here,

120
00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:14.910
but by saving every last drop
of water and using it wisely,

121
00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:17.810
the city was able to make
the foliage flourish.

122
00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:20.950
Unfortunately, that stopped when the rain did.

123
00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:22.740
Not a single drop
of water has fallen

124
00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:25.920
in any part of this country
for three years now.

125
00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:26.800
Three years?!

126
00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:28.120
Wow, that long?

127
00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:30.020
But wait, even without rain,

128
00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:32.520
there was still the river as another water source.

129
00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:33.790
And it's close.

130
00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:36.120
Why couldn't they just pipe
the water in from over there?

131
00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:38.850
Well, the answer to that is just up ahead.

132
00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:40.180
[USOPP]
Hm?

133
00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:44.520
[VIVI]
Even though it's
a desert kingdom,

134
00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:47.080
never in a thousands of years
of Alabasta's history

135
00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:49.360
has the rain ever
stopped completely.

136
00:07:49.390 --> 00:07:51.330
However, there was one place in the country

137
00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:54.930
where the rain fell more than
usual, much more in fact.

138
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.240
Alubarna, the capital.

139
00:07:57.270 --> 00:08:00.270
The city where the king's palace is located.

140
00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:07.130
<b>2 Years Ago</b>

141
00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:23.000
[VIVI]
The people of the land
called it the "King's Miracle."

142
00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:26.400
At least, they did until
one particular day.

143
00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:31.160
<b>Port Town (Nanohana)</b>

144
00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.360
[SAILOR]
Get that cargo unloaded!

145
00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:30.730
We've got a schedule to keep!

146
00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.160
[STRIPED SHIRT]
We're losing it!

147
00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:39.870
Watch out!

148
00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:44.140
[CITIZEN I]
What happened?!
Is everyone all right?!

149
00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:48.170
<b>Half
Fledged</b>

150
00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.610
Damn it. What are we
supposed to do now?

151
00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:48.040
It's a delivery for the king.

152
00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:50.180
What's he gonna do when it doesn't arrive on time?

153
00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:50.050
<b>Half
Fledged</b>

154
00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.140
[CITIZEN J]
This green powder's
for the king?

155
00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:53.180
What is it?

156
00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.220
[BILLIONS A]
What is it?

157
00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:55.780
How the hell should we know?!

158
00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:57.990
We're only following your king's orders.

159
00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:00.190
[BILLIONS B]
We're just couriers!

160
00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:01.560
Run!

161
00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:07.920
[CITIZEN K]
Wait a minute. Could this be...?

162
00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.730
[NAMI]
Dance Powder?

163
00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.740
Oh, so you've heard of it?

164
00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:13.880
Yes.

165
00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:16.680
I sure have. It summons rain.

166
00:09:16.710 --> 00:09:17.850
A powder can?

167
00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:19.720
[NAMI]
I've only heard
stories about it,

168
00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:22.250
but apparently, dance powder
was created by a researcher

169
00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:24.220
in a country where
it never rained.

170
00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:28.020
Burning it creates a misty
smoke which rises into the sky.

171
00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:30.590
Once it reaches the clouds, it causes them to rain.

172
00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:32.060
In essence, it gives
you the ability

173
00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:34.600
to create rain on the spot.

174
00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.130
You'd think so.

175
00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.130
In fact, as its name suggests,

176
00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:39.700
the country that developed dance powder

177
00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:41.440
was happy enough to dance.

178
00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:42.800
It got lots of rain.

179
00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:43.640
But there was a catch:

180
00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:46.610
Its neighboring country had a drought.

181
00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:48.430
Let me explain how it works.

182
00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:49.610
Now...

183
00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:51.480
The mist from the
burned dance powder

184
00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:54.330
targets small clouds that aren't ready to rain yet.

185
00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:57.400
It artificially matures them into full rain clouds.

186
00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:59.220
Those clouds would have naturally grown

187
00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.090
into rain clouds,

188
00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:02.220
but when they were
further downwind...

189
00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:03.260
[USOPP]
Oh, I get it!

190
00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:05.260
It steals all the rain that
would've normally gone

191
00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:06.530
to a neighboring country!

192
00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:08.400
That musta caused
some big problems!

193
00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:09.730
[NAMI]
Oh, it did.

194
00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:12.300
A war broke out between the two countries.

195
00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:13.400
Ever since then,

196
00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:16.440
the World Government has
instituted a worldwide ban

197
00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:19.140
on the production and
possession of dance powder.

198
00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:22.920
[USOPP]
Even so, some of it
managed to show up here, huh.

199
00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:23.990
When it happened,

200
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:27.230
the country had been
experiencing strange weather.

201
00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:28.690
There had been no rain.

202
00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:31.800
Not a single drop had fallen
anywhere except one place,

203
00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:34.440
and that was the capital.

204
00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:36.680
[CITIZEN L]
No wonder we haven't had
any rain in ages!

205
00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:39.520
The king stole it for the capital
using this dance powder!

206
00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.760
[CITIZEN M]
So Alubarna's rain
wasn't a miracle at all!

207
00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:43.030
It was a sham!

208
00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:43.460
Yeah!

209
00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:45.740
[CITIZEN N]
Yeah! One that's left us parched and starving!

210
00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:47.530
This is all King Cobra's fault!

211
00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:51.570
Vivi! That means your
dad is the bad guy here!

212
00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:53.740
No! You idiot! He was framed!

213
00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:54.520
[LUFFY]
Ow! Ow!

214
00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:56.890
[SANJI]
Her sweet dear old dad
would never do such a thing,

215
00:10:58.330 --> 00:10:59.560
you got it?

216
00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:04.600
Of course. My father didn't
have anything to do with it.

217
00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.740
He was innocent.

218
00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:09.580
Unfortunately, a large
amount of dance powder

219
00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:12.780
was discovered inside his
palace shortly thereafter.

220
00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:13.890
[ZORO]
Huh.

221
00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:17.760
They even had people working inside the palace.

222
00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:20.900
[SANJI]
So... what is this? A road?

223
00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:23.000
No. It used to be a large canal.

224
00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:26.390
It piped in fresh water
from the Sandora River.

225
00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:27.920
Until someone destroyed it.

226
00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:29.880
Now do you see what happened?

227
00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:31.180
With its canal gone,

228
00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:35.520
the City of Green lost its only
remaining source of fresh water.

229
00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:38.190
The people here
waited and prayed,

230
00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:40.320
but sadly, rain never came.

231
00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.510
[clatter]

232
00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:43.610
[NAMI]
Wow.

233
00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:45.530
Something like that
and the dance powder incident

234
00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:48.400
would really make people
distrust their king.

235
00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:51.370
[ZORO]
That's exactly what
Crocodile planned, I bet.

236
00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:52.700
[VIVI]
With no more water,

237
00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:55.370
fighting began to
break out in Erumalu.

238
00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:56.550
To escape the violence here,

239
00:11:56.580 --> 00:12:00.220
there was only one thing the exhausted citizens could do.

240
00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:01.690
They abandoned the city

241
00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:04.760
and left for other oases
in search of water.

242
00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:08.370
And then...

243
00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:12.670
[VIVI]
the City of
Green withered away.

244
00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:16.930
Someone's collapsed!

245
00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:20.230
Wait, you mean there are still
people living in this city?!

246
00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:32.650
[VIVI]
What did my father...

247
00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:33.840
and all of the
other good people...

248
00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:36.850
What did they ever do?

249
00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:38.850
They don't deserve this.

250
00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:40.450
It's hard enough to live in the desert.

251
00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:42.840
Every day, it's a struggle
just to survive.

252
00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:45.420
Somehow the people of Alabasta
found a way to do it

253
00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:47.450
and they led happy lives!

254
00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:50.140
But Crocodile
destroyed those lives!

255
00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:53.150
What gives him the right
to do that?! What?!

256
00:12:53.180 --> 00:12:55.350
All the while, as one of the Seven Warlords,

257
00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:58.130
he passes himself off
as a hero of the people!

258
00:12:58.130 --> 00:12:59.630
They don't know what
he's really doing!

259
00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:01.760
No one realizes that
he's actually deceiving

260
00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:05.230
the entire country,
even as they cheer him on!

261
00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:07.570
[CROWD]
– Crocodile! Crocodile!
– Crocodile! Crocodile!

262
00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:10.440
– Crocodile! Crocodile!
– Crocodile! Crocodile!

263
00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:14.410
I can't! I can't let
him get away with this!

264
00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:16.150
[LUFFY yells]

265
00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:27.060
Oh, well... Hope that
made him feel better.

266
00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:39.240
[LUFFY]
Vivi!

267
00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:41.570
Let's get movin', 'kay?

268
00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:43.760
I'm itchin' to do this!

269
00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:48.450
[NAMI]
He's right. Let's get to Yuba.

270
00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:52.280
That's where the rebel
army is, right? Yuba?

271
00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:53.700
Yes, I have to stop them.

272
00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:55.940
I'm going to persuade their leader.

273
00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:56.870
How so?

274
00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:58.730
I'll tell the rebel
leader the truth,

275
00:13:58.760 --> 00:14:01.230
that all of this is
Crocodile's doing,

276
00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:04.640
and have him stop all of
this pointless bloodshed.

277
00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:06.340
Let's go.

278
00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:25.390
[LUFFY groaning]

279
00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:29.530
I'm burning up.

280
00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:32.960
I don't think can't
even sweat anymore.

281
00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.370
Will you please spare us the melodramatics, Luffy?

282
00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:37.040
You're only gonna
wear yourself out.

283
00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:38.140
[LUFFY groans]

284
00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:40.140
Gee, I guess he's not listening.

285
00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:42.710
[CHOPPER groaning]

286
00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:44.540
Can't go on.

287
00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:46.480
Can't take hot weather.

288
00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:49.350
I'm fine in cold weather.

289
00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:50.720
It's because of all that fur.

290
00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:55.090
Why don't you take off that stupid reindeer costume?

291
00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:58.230
What did you just say
to me, big nose?!

292
00:14:58.230 --> 00:14:59.230
Don't make fun of reindeer!

293
00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:01.720
Monster!

294
00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:02.810
Chopper!

295
00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:05.480
Don't turn yourself big,
or I'm gonna quit pulling you.

296
00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:08.150
Who are you callin' a monster,
you bird-nosed freak?

297
00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:10.760
You better take it easy on
the nose, or I'll have to get tough!

298
00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:13.100
Turn small, will ya?

299
00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:20.560
Hey, the desert doesn't seem to bother you much, Vivi.

300
00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:22.430
Well, I was born and raised in this country,

301
00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:26.040
so I guess you could say I'm used to it.

302
00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:29.340
[USOPP]
So... what's
with all these hills?

303
00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:32.240
I was expecting a desert
to be more flat.

304
00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:33.580
[LUFFY]
Ugh!

305
00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:35.460
[VIVI]
This is a very old desert.

306
00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:38.330
Some of the sand dunes here are over 900 feet high.

307
00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:40.360
Nine hundred feet? Oh my God.

308
00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:45.090
No. That's... Ugh.
That's a mountain!

309
00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:47.460
[LUFFY]
So hot. Water.

310
00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:51.230
[NAMI]
Just one drink, Luffy.
Just one mouthful.

311
00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:53.940
Don't drink so much!

312
00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:56.710
Idiot! You'd better save some
of that water for Usopp!

313
00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:59.540
Hold on! You just had some!
I'm next! Gimme...

314
00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:00.810
Stop it, you guys!

315
00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:02.410
You're only going to
wear yourselves out

316
00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:03.380
if you keep it up!

317
00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:04.420
[LUFFY]
Hey, she started it!

318
00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:07.590
[USOPP]
It's always his fault!

319
00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:11.610
[LUFFY]
Hey, Sanji!

320
00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:13.750
Let's have one of
those box lunches!

321
00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:17.420
[SANJI]
Not yet. Not until Vivi says so.

322
00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:18.820
Come on, Vivi, how 'bout it?

323
00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:21.060
Let's eat! Doesn't
that sound good?

324
00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:23.460
But we're not even a tenth
of the way to Yuba, Luffy,

325
00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:25.930
and we have to make our
supplies last the whole way.

326
00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:29.430
Don't be silly, Vivi. Haven't
you heard the old proverb?

327
00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:31.500
"Make sure you eat
whenever you're hungry!"

328
00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:34.000
Oh, quit makin' things
up, you big fat liar!

329
00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:36.000
Okay, if you're that hungry,
I'll tell you what,

330
00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:38.680
at the next group
of rocks we come to?

331
00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:40.180
All right, rocks it is!

332
00:16:40.210 --> 00:16:42.580
Onward to the next group of rocks!

333
00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:44.680
'Kay, guys, whoever wins
at rock-paper-scissors

334
00:16:44.680 --> 00:16:46.050
has to carry everybody's stuff!

335
00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:47.560
[USOPP]
Quit deciding things!

336
00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:49.270
And ready... go!

337
00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:51.170
Rock! Paper! Scissors!

338
00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:51.870
[SANJI]
Wait!

339
00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:53.100
[NAMI]
Now just hold on!

340
00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:54.200
[ZORO]
Hey! You started late!

341
00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.210
[LUFFY laughs]

342
00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:56.240
[LUFFY]
I win!

343
00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.680
[NAMI]
Idiot.

344
00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:03.590
[LUFFY]
Heavy... So heavy...

345
00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:08.450
[LUFFY]
Why am I doin' all the work?

346
00:17:08.450 --> 00:17:10.280
[SANJI]
You said the winner carries all.

347
00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:11.180
Now shut up and haul.

348
00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:13.690
[NAMI]
Make sure you don't drop anything!

349
00:17:19.110 --> 00:17:21.580
Hey, guys! I spotted
rocks, dead ahead!

350
00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:23.020
You mean it?

351
00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:26.220
It's lunchtime! Let's eat!

352
00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:28.920
Whoa! That's so fast!

353
00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:37.700
[LUFFY]
Shade! It feels so good!

354
00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:43.600
[groaning]

355
00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:45.100
[LUFFY]
Hm?

356
00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:58.400
I need help!

357
00:17:58.470 --> 00:17:59.670
[USOPP]
That's weird.
Why is he coming back?

358
00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:02.510
There's a whole flock
of injured birds here that can't move!

359
00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:05.510
We need a doctor! Chopper!

360
00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:07.920
[LUFFY]
All right! Let's go, Chopper!

361
00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:09.620
[CHOPPER]
Coming!

362
00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:11.590
[LUFFY]
We gotta help those birds!

363
00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:12.390
What birds?

364
00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:13.390
Wait a minute, Luffy,

365
00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.960
those birds might not be
what you think they are!

366
00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:20.370
[LUFFY yells]

367
00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:22.040
[ZORO]
All of our stuff is gone!

368
00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:24.870
[NAMI]
We've been had!

369
00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:26.070
But I saw them!

370
00:18:26.110 --> 00:18:29.680
There was a whole flock of dying birds lying right there!

371
00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:33.880
I'm so sorry. I should've
mentioned this earlier.

372
00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:36.880
Warusagi birds are desert
bandits that deceive travelers

373
00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:38.690
and steal their belongings.

374
00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:41.890
[LUFFY]
You've gotta be kidding!

375
00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:46.130
You mean these birds play dead?
What a lousy buncha crooks!

376
00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:47.630
[VIVI]
This is all my fault!

377
00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:49.630
Those birds tricked me!

378
00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:52.400
Luffy, you dolt, is that all
you have to say for yourself?

379
00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:54.800
There were three days' worth
of supplies in those packs,

380
00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:57.070
and you just had to go and
let a bunch of stupid birds

381
00:18:57.140 --> 00:18:59.510
rob us blind in the
middle of a desert!

382
00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:01.500
How are we supposed to
get across this wasteland

383
00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:03.000
without food or water?

384
00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:05.040
I hope you're proud of yourself!

385
00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:08.550
Come on, it's not my fault.
I mean, they outsmarted me!

386
00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:10.880
You mean you're dumber than a bird?

387
00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:12.090
What's that?

388
00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:13.700
Knock it off, you two!

389
00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:15.260
[SANJI]
No, you're not that smart!

390
00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:17.100
Just save your energy.

391
00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:20.520
At times like this, it's better
just to let them have it out.

392
00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:22.300
[SANJI]
You're just a moron!

393
00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:24.310
Fine with me.

394
00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:25.500
Let's just take a break.

395
00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:29.320
This heat is just startin' to
wear on everybody's nerves.

396
00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:31.650
I'm sure we'll manage
food- and water-wise.

397
00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:33.270
It's nothin' that'll
kill us right away.

398
00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:35.270
Let's put it out of
our minds for now.

399
00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:36.410
Yeah, that's a good idea,

400
00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:38.940
because when I think about it, I get really thirsty.

401
00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:41.550
[CHOPPER]
Mh-hm.

402
00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:46.580
[cawing]

403
00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:50.860
[LUFFY yells]
[SANJI gasps]

404
00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:55.560
Give us our stuff
back, you thieves!

405
00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:59.070
No, Luffy! Don't chase them!

406
00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:00.210
That idiot.

407
00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:02.640
[NAMI]
Wait! Will you be
able to find your way back?

408
00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:06.350
[USOPP]
Get back here, you dope! Luffy!

409
00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:08.550
[LUFFY panting]

410
00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:12.420
[LUFFY]
Stop! You can't
get away from me!

411
00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:19.430
[LUFFY]
Get back here!

412
00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:26.330
Come on, Luffy. Hurry it up!

413
00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:29.320
Um, you don't suppose he could be lost, do you?

414
00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:31.230
And there are still so
many desert dangers

415
00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:33.700
I haven't had a chance to warn him about yet.

416
00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:37.660
[CHOPPER]
What's that?

417
00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:45.740
What on earth is that rumbling?

418
00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:50.770
[LUFFY laughing]

419
00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:55.780
[USOPP]
Is it another sandstorm?

420
00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:58.380
No, wait. That looks like–

421
00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:00.780
[USOPP gasps]

422
00:21:00.850 --> 00:21:02.020
It's Luffy!

423
00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:05.120
Oh, no. It can't be!

424
00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:07.350
[NAMI]
Huh?

425
00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:09.680
Why is he on a camel?

426
00:21:09.750 --> 00:21:12.020
[BOTH screaming]

427
00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:14.490
Someone wanna tell me what
the hell's chasing him?

428
00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:15.520
I can't really tell,

429
00:21:15.590 --> 00:21:17.360
but it looks like there's
something in the sand

430
00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:19.190
burrowing after him!

431
00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:25.830
What is that?

432
00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:27.560
It's a Sandora Dragon!

433
00:21:27.630 --> 00:21:28.330
[USOPP]
It's a what?

434
00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:30.000
[VIVI]
A Sandora Dragon!

435
00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:32.300
They're the biggest reptile
that lives in the desert!

436
00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:33.940
They wait under the
sand for their prey,

437
00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:35.240
and then ambush them!

438
00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:37.080
They have razor-sharp fangs and claws,

439
00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:38.920
but they hardly ever use them.

440
00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:40.750
Because they're so incredibly huge,

441
00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:43.890
they usually just end up
swallowing their victims whole!

442
00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:46.090
I gotta admit, that boy
does have a talent

443
00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:47.860
for attracting trouble.

444
00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:50.020
Right, and all of us have the scars to prove it.

445
00:21:50.060 --> 00:21:52.160
What kinda crap star
was he born under

446
00:21:52.190 --> 00:21:54.060
to attract trouble like that?

447
00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:57.160
[LUFFY]
Stop, camel,
you're going too fast!

448
00:21:57.890 --> 00:22:00.060
[ZORO]
Is he too much for you, Luffy?

449
00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:01.330
[SANJI]
We'll lend a hand!

450
00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:04.330
Thanks, guys! I brought home
a little somethin' for dinner!

451
00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:05.230
Gum-Gum...

452
00:22:05.400 --> 00:22:07.200
[ZORO]
– Tatsu...
[SANJI]
– Epaule...

453
00:22:07.240 --> 00:22:08.170
[LUFFY]
– Whip!
[ZORO]
– Maki!

454
00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:09.410
[SANJI]
Shoot!

455
00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:13.480
[ALL gasp]

456
00:22:13.510 --> 00:22:15.980
[roars]

457
00:22:17.850 --> 00:22:19.150
You didn't have to go that far!

458
00:22:19.180 --> 00:22:20.150
Whenever those guys fight,

459
00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:23.350
it almost makes me
feel sorry for the monsters!

460
00:22:30.560 --> 00:22:31.630
This is convenient.

461
00:22:31.660 --> 00:22:34.730
These rocks are just like a natural frying pan.

462
00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:37.570
[ZORO]
So, now that we have a moment,

463
00:22:37.570 --> 00:22:39.470
what's the deal with the camel?

464
00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:40.400
[LUFFY]
I dunno.

465
00:22:40.470 --> 00:22:42.470
It was gettin' eaten
by the mystery plants

466
00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:44.200
while I was chasin' those birds.

467
00:22:44.240 --> 00:22:46.170
[NAMI]
It's obviously not a wild camel.

468
00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:49.080
[VIVI]
No, not with
a saddle and bridle.

469
00:22:50.720 --> 00:22:52.220
He's a passenger-carrying camel?

470
00:22:52.250 --> 00:22:54.650
That's sure gonna
make things lots easier!

471
00:22:54.690 --> 00:22:56.320
Yeah, that oughtta
be a real help.

472
00:22:56.360 --> 00:22:58.020
It looks like he could carry two.

473
00:22:58.060 --> 00:23:00.730
Camels do go hand-in-hand
with deserts.

474
00:23:00.880 --> 00:23:03.140
Great, I'll take
the first shift.

475
00:23:04.210 --> 00:23:05.810
[LUFFY]
Ow!

476
00:23:05.850 --> 00:23:08.150
"I'm a freedom-loving,
hard-boiled, yet compassionate,

477
00:23:08.180 --> 00:23:09.120
son of the desert!

478
00:23:09.150 --> 00:23:10.980
I'm very grateful to you
for having helped me

479
00:23:10.980 --> 00:23:12.150
outta that jam back there,

480
00:23:12.180 --> 00:23:13.850
and I'll be glad to give
some of you a ride,

481
00:23:13.990 --> 00:23:16.330
but I'm afraid I don't accept
male passengers!"

482
00:23:16.360 --> 00:23:18.900
[USOPP]
Yeah, at least
give Chopper a ride!

483
00:23:19.940 --> 00:23:22.210
[CHOPPER]
"I'm too macho!"

484
00:23:22.250 --> 00:23:26.120
[USOPP]
Why, you! Why, I oughtta
punch you in the nu–

485
00:23:26.120 --> 00:23:27.790
[NAMI]
I'm so sorry that my crewmates

486
00:23:27.860 --> 00:23:29.420
are a bunch of ill-bred louts!

487
00:23:29.460 --> 00:23:31.060
Now, what should we call you,

488
00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:32.860
you great big
precious camel, you?

489
00:23:32.860 --> 00:23:33.360
[LUFFY]
Idiot!

490
00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:34.060
[SANJI]
Moron!

491
00:23:34.060 --> 00:23:35.200
[USOPP]
Doofus!

492
00:23:35.200 --> 00:23:36.800
"Eyelash" it is, then!

493
00:23:36.800 --> 00:23:39.510
[ZORO]
Uh, how'd you arrive at that?

494
00:23:39.540 --> 00:23:41.470
[NAMI]
Okay! Climb on, Vivi!

495
00:23:41.510 --> 00:23:44.250
No, I'm fine. I can
still walk. Thanks.

496
00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:45.820
Just get on.

497
00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:46.950
[LUFFY]
Pervert camel!

498
00:23:46.990 --> 00:23:50.790
[USOPP, SANJI, LUFFY]
– Pervert camel! Pervert camel!
– Pervert camel! Pervert camel!

499
00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:51.760
This is great.

500
00:23:51.790 --> 00:23:53.370
We should be able to make better time now!

501
00:23:53.370 --> 00:23:55.340
We need to get to Yuba as fast as we can

502
00:23:55.370 --> 00:23:58.240
so we'll be able to talk to the rebel army.

503
00:23:58.340 --> 00:23:59.790
Giddyup, Eyelash!

504
00:23:59.790 --> 00:24:01.460
[ALL]
– Hey, wait for us!
– Hey, wait for us!

505
00:24:02.750 --> 00:24:03.950
[NAMI]
Hurry up, guys!

506
00:24:03.980 --> 00:24:06.850
If you get separated, you'll never leave the desert alive!

507
00:24:06.850 --> 00:24:07.690
[USOPP]
Well, thanks a lot!

508
00:24:07.810 --> 00:24:09.410
[SANJI]
I like this side of Nami too!

509
00:24:09.480 --> 00:24:10.550
[ZORO]
What else is new?

510
00:24:10.580 --> 00:24:11.820
[ACE]
After them! Hurry!

511
00:24:11.820 --> 00:24:12.380
[ZORO]
Chopper! Hop on!

512
00:24:12.380 --> 00:24:12.980
[CHOPPER]
Right!

513
00:24:12.980 --> 00:24:15.320
[BOYS]
– Wait for us!
– Wait for us!
